{
  "body_human_readable": "## Tesla's 2024 Global Sales Reach Nearly 1.8 Million Vehicles\n\nTesla sold approximately 1.79 million vehicles globally in 2024, marking a slight decrease from the previous year. This represents the first time in a dozen years that the electric vehicle giant has seen an annual sales decline. Despite a strong fourth quarter with 495,570 vehicles delivered, it wasn't enough to surpass 2023's total of 1.81 million.\n\nThe top-selling models for Tesla in 2024 were the Model Y and Model 3, which together accounted for the vast majority of sales. Specifically, the Model Y was the most popular, with 1.22 million units sold, followed by the Model 3 with 476,626 units. The more expensive Model X and S, along with the newly introduced Cybertruck, made up a smaller portion of the total sales, with only 23,640 of these models sold in the last quarter of the year.\n\nRegionally, the United States and China remained Tesla's two largest markets. In 2024, an estimated 674,924 Tesla vehicles were sold in the United States, while China accounted for nearly 603,664 vehicle sales.\n\nThe slight dip in overall sales for 2024 has been attributed to a number of factors, including an aging model lineup and increased competition in key markets like China, Europe, and the U.S. While Tesla's production for the year was 1.77 million vehicles, slightly less than its sales, the company's revenue for 2024 still reached $97.7 billion.",
